ntfsck: orphan relink fixes

- an orphan whose parent reference is stale is relinked after the others
  (with any orphans stacked on it), so a stale record cannot take the name
  of the current file
- index lookup returns its own status for 'already linked' and 'name
  clash' instead of relying on errno
- lost+found: a name clash is renamed to FSCK_#<mft> as a Win32 name; a
  clashing DOS name is dropped; a name already linked there is kept; a
  second name that would also become FSCK_#<mft> is dropped
- re-find the $FILE_NAME after wiping an orphan folder's index, so its
  names are not counted twice and fn is not a stale pointer; if it cannot
  be found, leave the record for the next round
- undo the index add if a later step fails (also when re-adding a missing
  index entry); if the undo fails, keep the name as linked

